00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:14,740
(Watch on KonFlix.vip)

1
00:00:04,876 --> 00:00:07,245
I don't want to do the dance.

2
00:00:07,312 --> 00:00:08,546
<i>Then ask to be removed.</i>

3
00:00:08,613 --> 00:00:10,315
<i>But that just doesn't fit my image.</i>

4
00:00:10,381 --> 00:00:11,549
<i>But apparently, Nobunaga</i>

5
00:00:11,616 --> 00:00:13,551
<i>actually ran away from a battle once.</i>

6
00:00:13,618 --> 00:00:15,553
But I don't think it's lame.

7
00:00:15,620 --> 00:00:17,388
<i>It's kind of cool how</i>

8
00:00:17,455 --> 00:00:19,190
<i>he bares all his weaknesses, huh?</i>

9
00:00:19,791 --> 00:00:20,792
<i>Saku,</i>

10
00:00:20,859 --> 00:00:21,993
‎PREVIOUSLY ON <i>‎TATSUKI: TOO KIND FOR SCHOOL</i>

11
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:23,361
<i>you can become Nobunaga too.</i>

12
00:00:23,428 --> 00:00:27,165
Saku! Go! You can do it!

13
00:00:30,568 --> 00:00:31,736
Yeah!

14
00:00:31,803 --> 00:00:34,105
Tatsuki! Sora jumped.

15
00:00:43,047 --> 00:00:44,482
YUKANAI

16
00:00:44,549 --> 00:00:46,918
IT'S ALMOST SUMMER VACATION!
WE WILL BE OPEN DURING SUMMER VACATION

17
00:00:46,985 --> 00:00:49,621
I will give you this award to honor
your achievements

18
00:00:49,687 --> 00:00:51,523
this past month.

19
00:00:51,589 --> 00:00:52,590
-Here are some beads.
-Check.

20
00:00:54,626 --> 00:00:56,094
Oh, you got me.

21
00:00:56,661 --> 00:00:57,495
Hey.

22
00:00:57,996 --> 00:01:00,131
I've been wondering for a while,
but who's that man?

23
00:01:01,332 --> 00:01:02,500
Oh, that's Mr. Eiraku.

24
00:01:02,567 --> 00:01:03,668
He comes every now and then

25
00:01:03,735 --> 00:01:06,237
to teach us all sorts of old-school games.

26
00:01:06,304 --> 00:01:07,605
He's not a strong player though,

27
00:01:07,672 --> 00:01:08,840
so he’s pretty popular.

28
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:10,742
I see.

29
00:01:12,577 --> 00:01:14,646
All right, it's time to clean up!

30
00:01:14,712 --> 00:01:17,382
We're in the middle of a good game,
so give us some time.

31
00:01:17,448 --> 00:01:18,650
But it's cleaning day.

32
00:01:18,716 --> 00:01:19,918
Meanie.

33
00:01:19,984 --> 00:01:21,286
Meanie.

34
00:01:22,687 --> 00:01:24,055
Oh no, the paint dripped.

35
00:01:24,556 --> 00:01:26,057
Oh no.

36
00:01:26,124 --> 00:01:28,660
It was turning out so well too.

37
00:01:29,627 --> 00:01:30,995
What a shocking failure.

38
00:01:31,062 --> 00:01:33,798
-Shock-man.
-It's okay. Let me see it.

39
00:01:34,365 --> 00:01:36,301
I'll show you how to fix it.

40
00:01:39,871 --> 00:01:42,340
And then…

41
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:45,176
Go like this.

42
00:01:47,779 --> 00:01:50,215
-Wow.
-It's so pretty.

43
00:01:50,281 --> 00:01:52,483
Everyone, it's almost time to clean up.

44
00:01:52,550 --> 00:01:53,918
Whoa, the demon is here.

45
00:01:53,985 --> 00:01:55,286
What?

46
00:01:55,353 --> 00:01:56,788
Who are you calling a demon?

47
00:01:56,854 --> 00:01:58,690
-So scary!
-Oh no!

48
00:01:58,756 --> 00:01:59,791
Come on.

49
00:01:59,857 --> 00:02:01,226
-Start cleaning up.
-Seiryu.

50
00:02:01,292 --> 00:02:02,760
Here. How about this?

51
00:02:02,827 --> 00:02:04,729
Wow.

52
00:02:04,796 --> 00:02:06,097
-It's amazing.
-Right?

53
00:02:06,164 --> 00:02:07,065
Let's add more color--

54
00:02:07,131 --> 00:02:08,533
Hurry up and clean!

55
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:10,969
Run, everyone! Run!

56
00:02:11,035 --> 00:02:12,637
Don't let her catch you!

57
00:02:12,704 --> 00:02:14,539
It says that
there's going to be a barbecue.

58
00:02:14,606 --> 00:02:16,541
This is the schedule
for the summer vacation.

59
00:02:16,608 --> 00:02:18,643
Make sure you hand it to your mom and dad.

60
00:02:18,710 --> 00:02:20,745
-I'm so excited for this.
-Me too!

61
00:02:20,812 --> 00:02:21,913
Bye.

62
00:02:21,980 --> 00:02:23,314
-Bye.
-Bye.

63
00:02:23,381 --> 00:02:24,582
Be careful.

64
00:02:24,649 --> 00:02:26,918
-Hello.
-Bye.

65
00:02:26,985 --> 00:02:28,786
Sorry I'm late.

66
00:02:29,354 --> 00:02:31,556
-Ms. Tachibana, you're here for a meeting?
-Yes.

67
00:02:33,224 --> 00:02:34,192
Sorry to make you wait.

68
00:02:34,259 --> 00:02:35,493
-Hello.
-Hello.

69
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:36,494
Mr. Tatsuki.

70
00:02:36,561 --> 00:02:38,496
-What?
-You've got paint on your face.

71
00:02:38,563 --> 00:02:39,998
You've got paint on you.

72
00:02:43,468 --> 00:02:45,336
-It's still there.
-Forget it.

73
00:02:46,037 --> 00:02:48,640
How is Nene doing?

74
00:02:48,706 --> 00:02:49,741
Well,

75
00:02:50,742 --> 00:02:52,710
I'd like to cancel
her enrollment after this month.

76
00:02:54,812 --> 00:02:55,647
Is that right?

77
00:02:55,713 --> 00:02:56,648
Yes.

78
00:02:57,348 --> 00:03:00,852
Lately, my daughter isn't keen
on coming here anymore.

79
00:03:02,520 --> 00:03:06,424
Whether she wants to come or not
is entirely up to her, so that's okay,

80
00:03:07,191 --> 00:03:08,459
but is she unwell or something?

81
00:03:08,526 --> 00:03:11,095
No, not really.

82
00:03:12,630 --> 00:03:15,333
<i>She pretty much</i>
<i>stays holed up in her room,</i>

83
00:03:15,833 --> 00:03:18,736
<i>but she somehow manages to make it</i>
<i>to cram school and piano lessons.</i>

84
00:03:19,537 --> 00:03:20,371
I see.

85
00:03:21,005 --> 00:03:23,541
So when she's not at those places,
she stays in her room?

86
00:03:23,608 --> 00:03:24,709
Yes.

87
00:03:26,044 --> 00:03:29,914
I just don't want her to end up
as a shut-in.

88
00:03:30,982 --> 00:03:32,717
That's worrisome, isn't it?

89
00:03:33,484 --> 00:03:34,319
Yes.

90
00:03:34,886 --> 00:03:37,889
But you know, maybe she's enjoying
being a shut-in.

91
00:03:38,823 --> 00:03:40,758
-What?
-Enjoying it?

92
00:03:40,825 --> 00:03:41,826
Yes.

93
00:03:43,461 --> 00:03:45,863
We actually have lots of events

94
00:03:45,930 --> 00:03:47,832
coming up this month,

95
00:03:47,899 --> 00:03:49,267
so please let Nene know.

96
00:03:50,835 --> 00:03:53,004
-Okay, will do.
-Thank you.

97
00:03:53,071 --> 00:03:54,639
-Thank you for your time.
-Thank you.

98
00:03:55,139 --> 00:03:56,607
I can see myself out.

99
00:03:57,108 --> 00:03:58,676
-Thank you.
-Take care.

100
00:03:58,743 --> 00:03:59,944
See you again.

101
00:04:03,781 --> 00:04:06,951
How does one enjoy being a shut-in?

102
00:04:10,288 --> 00:04:11,289
What?

103
00:04:12,123 --> 00:04:12,957
You don't know?

104
00:04:21,566 --> 00:04:23,401
I'm heading out now.

105
00:04:24,102 --> 00:04:26,504
Don't forget about
your piano lesson today.

106
00:04:26,571 --> 00:04:29,040
NENE

107
00:04:43,488 --> 00:04:45,556
-Here you go.
-Thank you.

108
00:04:47,925 --> 00:04:50,995
Mr. Sora Fujinaga
was discharged this morning.

109
00:04:51,562 --> 00:04:52,397
What?

110
00:04:54,665 --> 00:04:56,401
-Is that right?
-Yes.

111
00:05:06,611 --> 00:05:08,880
YUKANAI SUMMER VACATION EVENT

112
00:05:08,946 --> 00:05:12,116
DIAMOND ART
LOTS OF DIFFERENT DESIGNS TO CHOOSE FROM!

113
00:05:15,753 --> 00:05:17,789
-What's this?
-Where are you, Shi-chan?

114
00:05:17,855 --> 00:05:19,490
-Wait, I'm scared.
-Where are you?

115
00:05:19,557 --> 00:05:21,192
-I found you!
-Wait!

116
00:05:21,259 --> 00:05:22,760
-There she is!
-Hold on!

117
00:05:22,827 --> 00:05:25,863
-Hold on!
-Shi-chan, you're so bad at this.

118
00:05:25,930 --> 00:05:27,532
I wasn't able to do anything yet.

119
00:05:27,598 --> 00:05:29,267
-You have to attack.
-Who's playing next?

120
00:05:29,333 --> 00:05:31,702
I thought I was attacking.

121
00:05:31,769 --> 00:05:32,770
Tatsuki is super strong.

122
00:05:33,271 --> 00:05:34,539
Tatsuki is crazy good.

123
00:05:35,106 --> 00:05:36,340
Really?

124
00:05:40,378 --> 00:05:41,879
Hi, Nene.

125
00:05:44,749 --> 00:05:46,984
Hello Nene.

126
00:05:47,819 --> 00:05:48,953
Hello.

127
00:05:52,990 --> 00:05:54,859
-You're so hyper.
-Kurumi, you're so fast.

128
00:05:54,926 --> 00:05:55,760
I am, huh?

129
00:05:55,827 --> 00:05:57,295
I'm always fast.

130
00:05:58,729 --> 00:05:59,831
Hey Nene.

131
00:06:01,632 --> 00:06:03,000
We just started.

132
00:06:03,067 --> 00:06:04,135
Come join us.

133
00:06:05,269 --> 00:06:06,370
Sit here.

134
00:06:06,971 --> 00:06:08,306
Okay.

135
00:06:08,940 --> 00:06:09,774
You can start

136
00:06:09,841 --> 00:06:12,276
by placing the gems
on the mane and the tail.

137
00:06:12,844 --> 00:06:16,214
-You can't be sloppy with this.
-I'm intent on finishing this.

138
00:06:17,615 --> 00:06:19,784
-You're so detailed.
-Which gems do I use?

139
00:06:19,851 --> 00:06:20,985
Yeah, it's so pretty.

140
00:06:21,052 --> 00:06:22,053
Whichever one you want.

141
00:06:22,119 --> 00:06:23,454
You're right.

142
00:06:23,521 --> 00:06:24,722
Yeah.

143
00:06:28,926 --> 00:06:30,228
Tatsuki, can you choose for me?

144
00:06:34,065 --> 00:06:35,066
Then…

145
00:06:36,067 --> 00:06:37,702
You can use the example as a reference.

146
00:06:37,768 --> 00:06:39,303
-This pink color is so cute.
-Yeah.

147
00:06:42,006 --> 00:06:42,840
Here you go.

148
00:06:48,012 --> 00:06:50,314
Nene, will you be at the Yukanai Camp?

149
00:06:50,815 --> 00:06:51,649
Camp?

150
00:06:51,716 --> 00:06:53,885
Apparently, we're going to barbecue

151
00:06:53,951 --> 00:06:55,553
and do fireworks together.

152
00:06:55,620 --> 00:06:58,022
-That sounds like fun.
-Right?

153
00:06:58,089 --> 00:06:58,923
You should come.

154
00:06:58,990 --> 00:07:01,225
-Although we'll be staying the night here.
-Yeah.

155
00:07:01,726 --> 00:07:03,261
That's not so bad.

156
00:07:03,761 --> 00:07:06,697
But this is my last month here.

157
00:07:06,764 --> 00:07:07,965
Really?

158
00:07:08,032 --> 00:07:09,433
That's a bummer.

159
00:07:09,500 --> 00:07:10,334
Yeah.

160
00:07:10,401 --> 00:07:11,435
Oh no, I messed up.

161
00:07:12,737 --> 00:07:14,539
I did too. Look at mine.

162
00:07:14,605 --> 00:07:16,707
-It's not aligned.
-Right?

163
00:07:16,774 --> 00:07:17,642
Oh no.

164
00:07:17,708 --> 00:07:19,277
Wow Nene, you're so good.

165
00:07:20,278 --> 00:07:21,846
-Very nice.
-Looks good.

166
00:07:21,913 --> 00:07:23,481
-Yeah.
-You're so good.

167
00:07:23,548 --> 00:07:26,417
But what color should I choose
for the horse?

168
00:07:28,686 --> 00:07:30,087
You can choose whatever you want.

169
00:07:30,154 --> 00:07:31,656
I chose green for mine.

170
00:07:31,722 --> 00:07:33,124
That's very you, Mao.

171
00:07:33,190 --> 00:07:34,892
It's so pretty.

172
00:07:34,959 --> 00:07:36,761
I think I'll go with purple.

173
00:07:36,827 --> 00:07:38,462
-Nice.
-That'll look cool.

174
00:07:38,529 --> 00:07:40,064
Nene, what's your favorite color?

175
00:07:42,199 --> 00:07:43,768
My favorite color…

176
00:08:00,451 --> 00:08:01,986
I have to head to my piano lesson.

177
00:08:04,188 --> 00:08:06,023
You can finish this next time.

178
00:08:06,090 --> 00:08:07,692
But this is her last month, right?

179
00:08:07,758 --> 00:08:10,328
If she wants to come,
she can come again next month. Okay?

180
00:08:11,462 --> 00:08:12,496
Bye.

181
00:08:12,563 --> 00:08:13,631
Bye.

182
00:08:13,698 --> 00:08:15,166
Bye.

183
00:08:27,178 --> 00:08:28,245
YUKANAI

184
00:08:28,312 --> 00:08:29,280
Diamond art, huh?

185
00:08:29,347 --> 00:08:30,181
Yeah.

186
00:08:30,247 --> 00:08:31,549
They look good.

187
00:08:33,150 --> 00:08:33,985
This is

188
00:08:34,852 --> 00:08:37,254
the one that Nene Tachibana
was working on.

189
00:08:38,322 --> 00:08:40,024
That's the girl that's leaving this month?

190
00:08:40,091 --> 00:08:40,925
Yes.

191
00:08:41,492 --> 00:08:43,127
It's detailed and precise.

192
00:08:43,194 --> 00:08:45,763
She plays the piano, so she seems
to be good with her hands.

193
00:08:45,830 --> 00:08:46,998
I see.

194
00:08:48,232 --> 00:08:49,967
What did you think when you saw this?

195
00:08:51,302 --> 00:08:52,370
Well…

196
00:08:54,105 --> 00:08:56,874
I felt like…

197
00:08:57,675 --> 00:08:59,810
it's really constrained.

198
00:08:59,877 --> 00:09:00,711
Constrained?

199
00:09:01,712 --> 00:09:03,447
I told her to freely choose the gems,

200
00:09:03,514 --> 00:09:05,249
but she had a hard time deciding.

201
00:09:05,316 --> 00:09:07,385
I wonder why that is.

202
00:09:09,587 --> 00:09:11,022
Maybe

203
00:09:11,088 --> 00:09:14,959
she's scared to express herself
freely and as she pleases?

204
00:09:17,561 --> 00:09:19,830
She might be lacking self-confidence.

205
00:09:23,601 --> 00:09:25,736
-What is it?
-Oh.

206
00:09:26,971 --> 00:09:28,205
Watching Nene

207
00:09:28,839 --> 00:09:31,275
<i>reminded me of Sora for some reason.</i>

208
00:09:38,482 --> 00:09:39,684
How's your son doing?

209
00:09:41,852 --> 00:09:44,288
It seems like he was discharged
from the hospital.

210
00:09:44,789 --> 00:09:45,690
That's all I know.

211
00:09:46,257 --> 00:09:47,358
-I see.
-Yeah.

212
00:09:50,828 --> 00:09:53,330
Tatsuki, you need a good night's rest.

213
00:09:53,397 --> 00:09:54,565
-Okay?
-Yeah.

214
00:10:11,015 --> 00:10:12,850
The competition is coming up soon.

215
00:10:14,618 --> 00:10:15,519
How's it going?

216
00:10:16,187 --> 00:10:18,155
Do you think
you can do pretty well this time?

217
00:10:20,157 --> 00:10:21,258
Not sure.

218
00:10:22,126 --> 00:10:24,829
Your teacher said you'll do well
if you keep up the good work.

219
00:10:26,397 --> 00:10:29,366
But I'm not as good as Big Sis.

220
00:10:30,735 --> 00:10:33,270
There's no need
to compare yourself to her.

221
00:10:33,771 --> 00:10:35,172
After all, you're you.

222
00:10:36,540 --> 00:10:38,309
-Okay?
-Okay.

223
00:10:47,418 --> 00:10:50,354
I went to Yukanai today.

224
00:10:51,155 --> 00:10:51,989
What?

225
00:10:52,523 --> 00:10:53,357
Why?

226
00:10:54,225 --> 00:10:55,359
I did some diamond art.

227
00:10:58,028 --> 00:10:58,963
Is that right?

228
00:11:07,638 --> 00:11:08,472
Nene,

229
00:11:09,540 --> 00:11:11,542
I've signed you up
for the summer study camp.

230
00:11:12,209 --> 00:11:13,043
-What?
-What?

231
00:11:14,011 --> 00:11:16,147
The cram school study camp?

232
00:11:16,213 --> 00:11:17,148
Yeah.

233
00:11:17,882 --> 00:11:20,284
You didn't do well
on that practice test the other day.

234
00:11:20,918 --> 00:11:23,053
There's no need to pressure her
about it right now.

235
00:11:24,054 --> 00:11:26,290
If she doesn't make up ground
during summer break,

236
00:11:26,357 --> 00:11:27,324
she'll fall behind.

237
00:11:27,391 --> 00:11:29,226
She hasn't even been able to go to school.

238
00:11:29,794 --> 00:11:32,496
I don't want to push her too hard
with things like study camp.

239
00:11:32,563 --> 00:11:33,664
Then

240
00:11:34,165 --> 00:11:36,167
is it okay if her grades keep dropping?

241
00:11:38,335 --> 00:11:40,437
The piano competition is coming up soon,

242
00:11:40,938 --> 00:11:44,275
so I want her to focus on that right now.

243
00:11:44,341 --> 00:11:46,110
You prefer that too, right Nene?

244
00:11:50,848 --> 00:11:52,449
It's better to focus on her studies.

245
00:11:53,017 --> 00:11:55,553
-Is it really so?
-What about the entrance exam?

246
00:11:55,619 --> 00:11:56,453
She won't take it?

247
00:11:57,288 --> 00:11:58,422
That's not what I'm saying.

248
00:12:00,825 --> 00:12:01,759
Nene.

249
00:12:02,426 --> 00:12:03,360
What do you want to do?

250
00:12:08,766 --> 00:12:09,700
YUKANAI

251
00:12:09,767 --> 00:12:10,701
NOW ACCEPTING NEW STUDENTS

252
00:12:14,238 --> 00:12:15,072
Hey!

253
00:12:15,139 --> 00:12:16,140
Anybody there?

254
00:12:16,207 --> 00:12:17,908
-What?
-Coming.

255
00:12:17,975 --> 00:12:19,844
-Help me.
-I'm coming.

256
00:12:19,910 --> 00:12:21,078
-I'll help.
-Here.

257
00:12:23,380 --> 00:12:24,882
What's all this?

258
00:12:24,949 --> 00:12:27,351
They're tents
for the Yukanai Camp next week!

259
00:12:27,418 --> 00:12:29,687
I had some extras at home in storage.

260
00:12:30,421 --> 00:12:32,990
Camping is all about the tent, right?

261
00:12:33,057 --> 00:12:35,693
Just pitching them in the yard
will really set the mood.

262
00:12:35,759 --> 00:12:36,994
Yeah.

263
00:12:37,061 --> 00:12:39,763
I guess we need to start
making preparations too.

264
00:12:39,830 --> 00:12:40,865
Right.

265
00:12:40,931 --> 00:12:43,234
We have to get ingredients
for the barbecue.

266
00:12:43,300 --> 00:12:45,402
-I want to do fireworks too.
-Sounds fun.

267
00:12:45,469 --> 00:12:46,570
What will you do, Ajicchan?

268
00:12:46,637 --> 00:12:47,671
Sweets workshop.

269
00:12:47,738 --> 00:12:49,807
We're planning to make ice cream together.

270
00:12:49,874 --> 00:12:51,775
That sounds fun. What about you, Soya?

271
00:12:51,842 --> 00:12:54,278
I'll be doing
a late-night gaming tournament.

272
00:12:54,345 --> 00:12:56,247
I'm seriously going to win.

273
00:12:56,313 --> 00:12:57,982
I will be in charge of stargazing.

274
00:12:59,316 --> 00:13:00,918
There are lots of participants this year,

275
00:13:00,985 --> 00:13:02,086
so I'm looking forward to it!

276
00:13:02,152 --> 00:13:03,988
I don't see Nene these days,
but is she coming?

277
00:13:04,054 --> 00:13:06,257
She'll be leaving
at the end of this month.

278
00:13:06,824 --> 00:13:08,058
I see.

279
00:13:08,125 --> 00:13:10,761
I'll try to at least
extend another invitation.

280
00:13:11,862 --> 00:13:14,531
Maybe I'll ask Shi-chan
to be the camp leader this year.

281
00:13:16,467 --> 00:13:18,702
Do you think I can handle
such an important role?

282
00:13:18,769 --> 00:13:20,771
-Shouldn't it be Mr. Tatsuki instead?
-No.

283
00:13:20,838 --> 00:13:22,673
Tatsuki isn't cut out
for that kind of stuff.

284
00:13:24,141 --> 00:13:24,975
Then

285
00:13:25,676 --> 00:13:26,677
Mr. Tatsuki,

286
00:13:26,744 --> 00:13:29,413
-you're in charge of the barbecue.
-Huh?

287
00:13:29,480 --> 00:13:30,314
What do I have to do?

288
00:13:30,381 --> 00:13:31,815
Buy the ingredients,

289
00:13:31,882 --> 00:13:33,717
then prepare and cook
on the day of the event.

290
00:13:33,784 --> 00:13:36,020
-We'll be counting on you.
-I have to do that alone?

291
00:13:36,086 --> 00:13:37,054
Yes.

292
00:13:37,121 --> 00:13:38,455
-What?
-Good luck.

293
00:13:39,156 --> 00:13:41,692
That'll be impossible!

294
00:13:42,860 --> 00:13:44,361
Hello, this is Tachibana.

295
00:13:45,095 --> 00:13:46,830
This is Aomine from Yukanai.

296
00:13:47,865 --> 00:13:49,066
-Hello.
<i>-Um…</i>

297
00:13:49,133 --> 00:13:51,802
An event called Yukanai Camp
is coming up, can Nene attend

298
00:13:51,869 --> 00:13:54,038
before she leaves at the end of the month?

299
00:13:55,272 --> 00:13:56,240
I'm sorry.

300
00:13:56,307 --> 00:13:58,375
She's going to be at a study camp
on that day.

301
00:13:59,510 --> 00:14:00,544
I see.

302
00:14:00,611 --> 00:14:02,947
-Thank you for your time.
<i>-Thank you.</i>

303
00:14:04,815 --> 00:14:06,183
Um…

304
00:14:06,250 --> 00:14:09,353
How has Nene been doing lately?

305
00:14:10,254 --> 00:14:12,489
She's doing well.

306
00:14:13,991 --> 00:14:15,326
I'm glad to hear that.

307
00:14:16,226 --> 00:14:18,362
Thank you for your time. Bye.

308
00:14:18,429 --> 00:14:19,997
<i>Bye.</i>

309
00:14:29,773 --> 00:14:30,774
Nene?

310
00:14:33,610 --> 00:14:35,245
-Tatsuki.
-Off to your piano lesson?

311
00:14:36,647 --> 00:14:38,716
-I have cram school today.
-I see.

312
00:14:40,551 --> 00:14:41,685
What were you doing?

313
00:14:43,520 --> 00:14:44,822
I'm out shopping

314
00:14:45,322 --> 00:14:46,457
to buy things for our camp.

315
00:14:46,523 --> 00:14:48,926
It's so heavy my arms are about
to fall off.

316
00:14:50,094 --> 00:14:51,195
I wish I could go.

317
00:14:52,162 --> 00:14:53,030
You should come.

318
00:14:55,032 --> 00:14:56,266
But I didn't sign up.

319
00:14:56,834 --> 00:14:58,502
You can still come.

320
00:14:58,569 --> 00:14:59,937
You can finish the diamond art.

321
00:15:02,172 --> 00:15:03,307
But

322
00:15:03,841 --> 00:15:05,642
I have to go to the study camp too.

323
00:15:07,211 --> 00:15:08,312
I see.

324
00:15:08,812 --> 00:15:11,281
EXAM PREP CRAM SCHOOL

325
00:15:13,650 --> 00:15:14,485
Bye.

326
00:15:15,919 --> 00:15:16,754
See you again.

327
00:15:28,699 --> 00:15:29,767
Nene.

328
00:15:32,903 --> 00:15:34,505
Want to work on the diamond art?

329
00:15:39,743 --> 00:15:41,011
Here you go.

330
00:15:43,580 --> 00:15:45,115
Use whatever color gem you want.

331
00:15:47,084 --> 00:15:48,986
Which color should I choose?

332
00:15:53,323 --> 00:15:54,258
Do you have gold?

333
00:15:55,826 --> 00:15:58,529
Gold?

334
00:15:59,463 --> 00:16:00,597
I don't think so.

335
00:16:02,366 --> 00:16:03,467
You like gold?

336
00:16:07,971 --> 00:16:10,107
Yeah, since it represents number one.

337
00:16:10,674 --> 00:16:11,675
I see.

338
00:16:14,578 --> 00:16:15,512
Then

339
00:16:16,080 --> 00:16:17,181
I'll make sure to buy it.

340
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:37,267
Thank you.

341
00:16:37,334 --> 00:16:38,769
You're welcome.

342
00:16:41,472 --> 00:16:44,808
Can I take this home once I finish?

343
00:16:44,875 --> 00:16:46,076
Of course.

344
00:16:47,611 --> 00:16:50,147
Your mom and dad will be surprised
with your masterpiece.

345
00:16:52,883 --> 00:16:56,420
But I'll get in trouble
for skipping cram school.

346
00:17:00,290 --> 00:17:01,125
Really?

347
00:17:06,964 --> 00:17:09,833
You used two different colors
for the horses, huh?

348
00:17:11,368 --> 00:17:12,970
-Is it weird?
-No.

349
00:17:13,470 --> 00:17:14,738
It's such a great idea.

350
00:17:17,040 --> 00:17:18,475
Why did you choose these colors?

351
00:17:24,448 --> 00:17:26,450
Mom likes pink,

352
00:17:28,552 --> 00:17:32,356
and I think this other color
will make Dad happy.

353
00:17:39,963 --> 00:17:40,831
That's nice.

354
00:18:10,260 --> 00:18:11,395
I'm home.

355
00:18:11,461 --> 00:18:12,396
Welcome back.

356
00:18:12,896 --> 00:18:13,730
‎I'm done.

357
00:18:15,299 --> 00:18:16,266
Nene,

358
00:18:17,334 --> 00:18:18,735
why didn't you go to cram school?

359
00:18:19,736 --> 00:18:21,672
They called to tell us you didn't show up.

360
00:18:23,307 --> 00:18:24,241
I'm sorry.

361
00:18:25,275 --> 00:18:26,543
Where've you been until now?

362
00:18:28,545 --> 00:18:29,379
Yukanai.

363
00:18:30,414 --> 00:18:31,348
Why?

364
00:18:31,848 --> 00:18:33,016
What were you doing there?

365
00:18:33,517 --> 00:18:36,386
We're fine with you going there,

366
00:18:36,987 --> 00:18:38,121
but just know this,

367
00:18:38,622 --> 00:18:40,090
you have responsibilities too.

368
00:18:47,030 --> 00:18:48,265
I'm sorry.

369
00:18:48,832 --> 00:18:52,436
I'm not asking
for anything difficult here.

370
00:18:52,502 --> 00:18:55,539
If school isn't a good fit for you,
then it's fine that you don't go.

371
00:18:55,606 --> 00:18:59,142
But in exchange, you need to go
to cram school and study.

372
00:18:59,643 --> 00:19:01,311
You're taking the entrance exam, right?

373
00:19:03,747 --> 00:19:07,684
And yet, if you go around saying
you can't do this and you can't do that,

374
00:19:08,418 --> 00:19:10,220
that's being unreasonable, isn't it?

375
00:19:11,421 --> 00:19:13,156
What do you plan to do from here on out?

376
00:19:13,223 --> 00:19:14,458
Let's not get into that now.

377
00:19:14,524 --> 00:19:15,826
Why not?

378
00:19:16,493 --> 00:19:18,395
I'm saying this for her sake.

379
00:19:18,462 --> 00:19:19,997
She can study

380
00:19:20,063 --> 00:19:22,299
at her own pace
and do it little by little.

381
00:19:22,366 --> 00:19:24,368
Things turned out this way

382
00:19:24,434 --> 00:19:26,103
because you keep coddling her like that.

383
00:19:26,169 --> 00:19:27,838
As if it's my fault?

384
00:19:27,904 --> 00:19:30,240
You keep on pressuring her like that
all the time…

385
00:19:30,307 --> 00:19:33,243
-So it's my fault?
-I didn't say that.

386
00:20:44,815 --> 00:20:49,252
Stack small pieces of charcoal
in a pyramid atop the fire starter…

387
00:20:49,786 --> 00:20:50,987
A pyramid?

388
00:20:52,222 --> 00:20:54,725
We got a call from Nene's mom.

389
00:20:54,791 --> 00:20:55,692
What did she say?

390
00:20:55,759 --> 00:20:56,927
She was upset.

391
00:20:57,427 --> 00:21:00,130
Were you aware
that Nene skipped cram school?

392
00:21:00,864 --> 00:21:03,600
‎-Yeah.
‎-No wonder she was upset.

393
00:21:03,667 --> 00:21:06,002
Nene didn't want to go,
so there's nothing I can do.

394
00:21:06,069 --> 00:21:07,070
Yeah…

395
00:21:07,137 --> 00:21:09,606
But even so, you should've
at least reported it.

396
00:21:09,673 --> 00:21:11,041
Hey everyone.

397
00:21:11,108 --> 00:21:12,843
-Hello.
-Hey.

398
00:21:13,610 --> 00:21:16,179
-Here's what you asked for.
-Thank you.

399
00:21:17,814 --> 00:21:19,349
Sixty colors should be enough, right?

400
00:21:19,416 --> 00:21:20,717
More than enough.

401
00:21:21,218 --> 00:21:22,319
By the way,

402
00:21:22,386 --> 00:21:25,021
what happened to Nene after that?

403
00:21:26,423 --> 00:21:30,026
She took the finished diamond art
home with her.

404
00:21:30,627 --> 00:21:31,528
I found it.

405
00:21:32,629 --> 00:21:33,530
Here it is.

406
00:21:35,866 --> 00:21:38,435
-She chose the colors pink and brown?
-Yes.

407
00:21:39,503 --> 00:21:44,341
‎She used brown and pink because
‎those are her parents' favorite colors.

408
00:21:45,275 --> 00:21:47,544
But I guess
they're not Nene's favorite colors.

409
00:21:48,812 --> 00:21:50,247
I wonder what this means.

410
00:21:57,154 --> 00:22:00,223
<i>She said that she likes the color gold.</i>

411
00:22:00,290 --> 00:22:02,492
But I wonder if she said that
with her parents in mind.

412
00:22:03,760 --> 00:22:05,095
I see.

413
00:22:05,796 --> 00:22:09,466
I wonder how she really feels about
leaving Yukanai.

414
00:22:13,036 --> 00:22:16,006
Should I go
visit Nene at her house tomorrow?

415
00:22:18,308 --> 00:22:21,745
It's better not to interfere too much
in other people's family matters.

416
00:22:21,812 --> 00:22:23,947
I have no intention
of interfering unnecessarily.

417
00:22:24,014 --> 00:22:25,649
Then why do you want to go there?

418
00:22:26,683 --> 00:22:27,984
Because…

419
00:22:29,453 --> 00:22:31,955
I just want to do whatever I can.

420
00:22:32,456 --> 00:22:36,860
After all, Yukanai might be
a precious place for Nene.

421
00:22:39,729 --> 00:22:42,299
Let's leave this up to Shi-chan for now.

422
00:22:45,001 --> 00:22:47,337
But be careful when dealing with Nene.

423
00:22:48,338 --> 00:22:49,206
Yes.

424
00:22:53,910 --> 00:22:54,744
Thank you

425
00:22:54,811 --> 00:22:57,180
for taking time to meet with me.

426
00:22:57,247 --> 00:22:58,215
My pleasure.

427
00:22:59,015 --> 00:23:03,820
But we still plan to leave Yukanai
at the end of this month.

428
00:23:03,887 --> 00:23:05,121
I'm sorry.

429
00:23:05,722 --> 00:23:06,556
No problem at all.

430
00:23:08,225 --> 00:23:09,493
Where is Nene right now?

431
00:23:11,795 --> 00:23:13,630
She's in her room.

432
00:23:13,697 --> 00:23:15,699
I just want to let her be for now.

433
00:23:16,466 --> 00:23:19,936
I think
she's a bit overwhelmed right now.

434
00:23:20,003 --> 00:23:20,837
NENE

435
00:23:20,904 --> 00:23:23,507
She's still going to cram school
and piano lessons, right?

436
00:23:24,107 --> 00:23:24,941
Yes.

437
00:23:26,009 --> 00:23:27,210
To be honest,

438
00:23:27,277 --> 00:23:30,413
I feel like cram school
is quite a burden for her.

439
00:23:30,914 --> 00:23:32,582
After all, she stopped going to school

440
00:23:32,649 --> 00:23:34,184
because she didn't enjoy studying.

441
00:23:35,452 --> 00:23:36,286
That’s why

442
00:23:36,853 --> 00:23:40,090
I think she should focus on piano,
since that's something she enjoys.

443
00:23:41,725 --> 00:23:43,860
Did Nene say that she enjoys it?

444
00:23:44,895 --> 00:23:46,897
I can tell just by watching her.

445
00:23:50,467 --> 00:23:51,301
I've decided

446
00:23:52,302 --> 00:23:54,638
to take a leave of absence from work.

447
00:23:56,139 --> 00:23:57,507
As a parent,

448
00:23:57,574 --> 00:24:00,810
I intend to face this issue with her
and help her out.

449
00:24:00,877 --> 00:24:02,212
So please rest assured.

450
00:24:06,349 --> 00:24:08,018
I'm sorry,

451
00:24:08,084 --> 00:24:11,021
-but can I use the restroom?
-Yes.

452
00:25:04,341 --> 00:25:06,142
YU

453
00:25:06,209 --> 00:25:08,712
I HEARD SORA WAS DISCHARGED,
BUT HOW'S HE DOING?

454
00:25:12,716 --> 00:25:13,883
Hey Sora!

455
00:25:18,188 --> 00:25:19,889
-Sora!
-Don't come in here!

456
00:25:19,956 --> 00:25:21,091
Go away!

457
00:25:22,726 --> 00:25:23,960
Open the door, Sora!

458
00:25:24,461 --> 00:25:25,395
Shut up!

459
00:25:56,893 --> 00:25:58,662
The study camp starts today, right?

460
00:26:00,163 --> 00:26:01,931
It's almost time to go.

461
00:26:01,998 --> 00:26:02,966
I wonder where she is.

462
00:26:07,437 --> 00:26:08,271
Hey.

463
00:26:09,005 --> 00:26:09,839
Are you ready to go?

464
00:26:11,007 --> 00:26:12,042
I'm coming in.

465
00:26:15,078 --> 00:26:17,280
What's the matter? Do you not feel well?

466
00:26:19,315 --> 00:26:20,283
I'm okay.

467
00:26:22,552 --> 00:26:23,887
I'll take you to the station.

468
00:26:23,953 --> 00:26:24,788
Let's hurry.

469
00:26:27,691 --> 00:26:28,525
Okay.

470
00:26:34,264 --> 00:26:35,832
Do your best.

471
00:26:37,567 --> 00:26:38,768
-Thanks.
-Sure.

472
00:26:50,914 --> 00:26:52,215
CRAM SCHOOL
FOR MIDDLE SCHOOL ENTRANCE EXAMS

473
00:26:52,282 --> 00:26:53,850
Good morning.

474
00:26:54,451 --> 00:26:55,285
Yes.

475
00:26:58,121 --> 00:26:59,522
YUKANAI

476
00:26:59,589 --> 00:27:01,524
YUKANAI CAMP

477
00:27:10,967 --> 00:27:11,901
All right.

478
00:27:11,968 --> 00:27:13,436
Hello!

479
00:27:13,503 --> 00:27:14,971
Hello!

480
00:27:16,439 --> 00:27:18,174
Hey!

481
00:27:18,241 --> 00:27:19,342
Let's play Mario Kart.

482
00:27:19,409 --> 00:27:20,577
There's a game in the evening.

483
00:27:20,643 --> 00:27:21,878
I want to practice for that.

484
00:27:21,945 --> 00:27:22,979
What?

485
00:27:23,046 --> 00:27:24,814
You're using me just to practice?

486
00:27:24,881 --> 00:27:25,949
-Don't forget.
-Attention!

487
00:27:26,015 --> 00:27:28,051
Whoever's free, come out to the yard.

488
00:27:28,118 --> 00:27:29,919
-Okay.
-Come help us.

489
00:27:29,986 --> 00:27:32,055
This will fit about four to five.

490
00:27:32,122 --> 00:27:33,723
This is exciting.

491
00:27:33,790 --> 00:27:36,726
I've been wanting to do stargazing.

492
00:27:36,793 --> 00:27:38,027
Do you know much about stars?

493
00:27:38,094 --> 00:27:40,096
Not at all. I only know the North Star.

494
00:27:40,930 --> 00:27:42,565
-I see.
-But

495
00:27:42,632 --> 00:27:44,968
there are apps that can help us out.

496
00:27:46,035 --> 00:27:47,537
I can search for the stars I want to see.

497
00:27:47,604 --> 00:27:49,005
That's so handy.

498
00:27:50,006 --> 00:27:50,907
The tent looks nice.

499
00:27:51,574 --> 00:27:52,976
Oh, it's a telescope!

500
00:27:53,042 --> 00:27:55,678
Yeah, Professor Mikumo brought this.

501
00:27:55,745 --> 00:27:56,980
-Wow.
-Yeah.

502
00:27:57,046 --> 00:27:58,782
I found it at a flea market.

503
00:27:58,848 --> 00:27:59,849
Hey,

504
00:27:59,916 --> 00:28:00,984
someone help me out.

505
00:28:01,551 --> 00:28:03,386
I'll help.

506
00:28:03,453 --> 00:28:04,554
Thanks, Umine.

507
00:28:04,621 --> 00:28:05,455
Then

508
00:28:05,522 --> 00:28:07,090
-can you bring the firewood?
-Firewood?

509
00:28:07,157 --> 00:28:08,057
-Yeah.
-This?

510
00:28:08,124 --> 00:28:08,958
Yeah, the same one.

511
00:28:09,025 --> 00:28:09,993
Okay.

512
00:28:10,059 --> 00:28:11,127
-Thanks.
-Tatsuki.

513
00:28:11,194 --> 00:28:12,495
Can I do the fireworks?

514
00:28:12,562 --> 00:28:15,298
Yeah, but it won't be as pretty
if you do it right now.

515
00:28:16,566 --> 00:28:18,735
We can stay awake
as long as we want today, right?

516
00:28:18,802 --> 00:28:20,303
Yup, as long as you want.

517
00:28:20,370 --> 00:28:21,971
Then I'll stay awake all night.

518
00:28:22,872 --> 00:28:25,141
People who say that
always fall asleep first.

519
00:28:25,208 --> 00:28:27,243
Keep shaking.

520
00:28:28,111 --> 00:28:30,146
All right.

521
00:28:30,213 --> 00:28:31,981
Let's take it out of the bag.

522
00:28:33,316 --> 00:28:34,751
-It's done!
-Wow!

523
00:28:34,818 --> 00:28:36,019
Wow.

524
00:28:36,085 --> 00:28:37,487
Let's all eat this tonight.

525
00:28:37,554 --> 00:28:39,656
Hooray!

526
00:28:39,722 --> 00:28:40,557
<i>Begin.</i>

527
00:28:40,623 --> 00:28:41,558
Go!

528
00:28:41,624 --> 00:28:43,626
Let's all eliminate Ei-chan first.

529
00:28:43,693 --> 00:28:44,727
Good idea.

530
00:28:44,794 --> 00:28:46,830
Don't bully the elderly.

531
00:28:47,931 --> 00:28:50,533
Hey, did Nene show up?

532
00:28:51,100 --> 00:28:52,202
Nope, she's not here.

533
00:28:52,769 --> 00:28:54,604
I see.

534
00:28:54,671 --> 00:28:56,039
-Thanks.
-Sure.

535
00:28:56,105 --> 00:28:57,507
Go for it.

536
00:28:57,574 --> 00:28:59,475
Go, go!

537
00:28:59,542 --> 00:29:00,410
You can do it.

538
00:29:00,476 --> 00:29:02,345
-You can do it.
-You can do it.

539
00:29:03,980 --> 00:29:05,548
What's wrong with this?

540
00:29:05,615 --> 00:29:06,716
Just a little bit more.

541
00:29:06,783 --> 00:29:09,018
We can't eat unless you get
the fire started.

542
00:29:09,085 --> 00:29:10,620
-Just wait a minute.
-How's it going?

543
00:29:11,187 --> 00:29:14,290
I piled the charcoal
in the form of a pyramid.

544
00:29:14,357 --> 00:29:15,592
-But…
-Oh.

545
00:29:15,658 --> 00:29:17,760
There's no way
air can pass through like this.

546
00:29:17,827 --> 00:29:18,962
Huh?

547
00:29:19,028 --> 00:29:20,163
You can do it.

548
00:29:20,230 --> 00:29:22,232
All right. It's ready.

549
00:29:22,866 --> 00:29:25,468
-Soya, you're a genius.
-Thank you.

550
00:29:25,535 --> 00:29:26,669
Good job.

551
00:29:28,438 --> 00:29:29,272
Okay.

552
00:29:29,339 --> 00:29:31,207
All right, let's start grilling.

553
00:29:34,077 --> 00:29:36,246
-It looks delicious.
-I can't wait to eat paella.

554
00:29:36,312 --> 00:29:37,814
Ready?

555
00:29:37,881 --> 00:29:39,549
Open sesame!

556
00:29:40,216 --> 00:29:41,451
It's paella.

557
00:29:41,517 --> 00:29:42,552
It looks so good.

558
00:29:42,619 --> 00:29:44,120
It's paella.

559
00:29:44,187 --> 00:29:45,688
It's so good!

560
00:29:45,755 --> 00:29:46,890
It's super yummy!

561
00:29:46,956 --> 00:29:48,925
I want to roast a marshmallow.

562
00:29:48,992 --> 00:29:51,027
I'm going to grill a sausage.

563
00:29:51,094 --> 00:29:52,395
-Go ahead.
-It's time

564
00:29:52,462 --> 00:29:54,297
-to grill some corn!
-Yay!

565
00:29:55,265 --> 00:29:58,001
It's time for corn.

566
00:29:58,067 --> 00:29:59,736
Where did Tatsuki go?

567
00:29:59,802 --> 00:30:00,803
Oh?

568
00:30:00,870 --> 00:30:01,938
He ran away, huh?

569
00:30:02,906 --> 00:30:04,941
Yup, he's not fit to be a leader at all.

570
00:30:31,367 --> 00:30:34,370
<i>The person you have called</i>
<i>is unable to answer right now…</i>

571
00:30:42,312 --> 00:30:44,147
YU

572
00:30:50,186 --> 00:30:51,020
Hello.

573
00:30:52,021 --> 00:30:53,957
I told you not to contact me anymore.

574
00:30:54,791 --> 00:30:55,725
How's Sora?

575
00:30:56,826 --> 00:30:58,294
How's he doing? Is he all right?

576
00:31:00,630 --> 00:31:01,731
You know…

577
00:31:03,566 --> 00:31:05,301
If you truly care about him,

578
00:31:05,802 --> 00:31:07,403
stay away from us forever.

579
00:31:33,563 --> 00:31:34,664
‎Hey.

580
00:31:35,631 --> 00:31:37,767
This was made
with gems of my favorite color.

581
00:31:38,267 --> 00:31:40,136
Tatsuki, you made this, right?

582
00:31:44,474 --> 00:31:45,508
That reminds me!

583
00:31:46,109 --> 00:31:47,510
Take a look at this.

584
00:31:51,247 --> 00:31:52,615
Ta-da!

585
00:31:53,583 --> 00:31:55,685
-It's beautiful.
-Isn't it?

586
00:31:56,552 --> 00:31:57,587
Go ahead and use it.

587
00:32:02,392 --> 00:32:03,693
I was supposed

588
00:32:05,728 --> 00:32:07,797
to go to the cram school study camp today.

589
00:32:09,265 --> 00:32:10,500
Good morning.

590
00:32:12,035 --> 00:32:12,969
I'm sorry,

591
00:32:15,238 --> 00:32:17,173
but I won't be going to the study camp.

592
00:32:17,874 --> 00:32:19,275
You decided not to go?

593
00:32:23,246 --> 00:32:24,747
I hate studying and playing the piano.

594
00:32:25,515 --> 00:32:26,349
What?

595
00:32:27,183 --> 00:32:28,451
I thought you liked piano.

596
00:32:29,118 --> 00:32:30,053
I hate it.

597
00:32:31,821 --> 00:32:32,822
I see.

598
00:32:35,024 --> 00:32:36,192
It must've been tough for you.

599
00:32:46,069 --> 00:32:46,903
Then,

600
00:32:49,372 --> 00:32:52,542
let's take time to enjoy this later.

601
00:32:52,608 --> 00:32:53,976
Let's enjoy the barbecue first.

602
00:32:54,844 --> 00:32:56,279
Hurry or there'll be no meat left.

603
00:32:58,514 --> 00:32:59,482
Let's go.

604
00:32:59,982 --> 00:33:02,585
All right, let's get ready
to crack the watermelon open.

605
00:33:03,086 --> 00:33:05,888
Here's another skewer.

606
00:33:05,955 --> 00:33:08,391
-Take one, Nene.
-Thank you.

607
00:33:08,958 --> 00:33:10,693
-Here you go.
-Thanks.

608
00:33:11,727 --> 00:33:13,463
What? Oh no.

609
00:33:14,030 --> 00:33:16,232
Oh no! It's stuck!

610
00:33:16,732 --> 00:33:19,102
You can remove it using baking soda.

611
00:33:19,669 --> 00:33:21,370
I need a different solution.

612
00:33:21,437 --> 00:33:23,606
Go! Go!

613
00:33:23,673 --> 00:33:25,908
Go! You can do it.

614
00:33:25,975 --> 00:33:28,544
Go! Go!

615
00:33:32,048 --> 00:33:33,649
Yeah!

616
00:33:33,716 --> 00:33:35,151
Let's try it.

617
00:33:35,651 --> 00:33:36,652
It's so good.

618
00:33:36,719 --> 00:33:37,753
It's really good.

619
00:33:40,690 --> 00:33:43,626
BLUE FLAME
JAPAN BLUE

620
00:33:49,565 --> 00:33:50,867
This one is so cute.

621
00:34:00,877 --> 00:34:02,044
How pretty.

622
00:34:19,095 --> 00:34:20,463
Your mom doesn't know you're here?

623
00:34:22,431 --> 00:34:24,300
She thinks I'm at study camp.

624
00:34:25,368 --> 00:34:27,436
That's not good.

625
00:34:27,937 --> 00:34:29,739
-I'm going to call your mom.
-Wait.

626
00:34:32,441 --> 00:34:33,643
Don't tell her.

627
00:34:35,344 --> 00:34:36,245
But

628
00:34:36,879 --> 00:34:38,314
your mom will be worried.

629
00:34:40,883 --> 00:34:42,418
I don't want to go home.

630
00:34:48,157 --> 00:34:49,725
Then you don't have to.

631
00:34:50,359 --> 00:34:52,228
I'll discuss it with your mom.

632
00:34:53,429 --> 00:34:54,430
Okay?

633
00:34:58,634 --> 00:35:01,003
What? She didn't go to study camp?

634
00:35:01,571 --> 00:35:02,738
Why?

635
00:35:02,805 --> 00:35:05,408
I just got a call telling me
that she's at Yukanai.

636
00:35:06,943 --> 00:35:08,578
-I'm going to go get her.
-Wait.

637
00:35:08,644 --> 00:35:09,545
What?

638
00:35:09,612 --> 00:35:12,915
There's a camping event
going on at Yukanai today, so she'll be

639
00:35:12,982 --> 00:35:13,950
staying the night.

640
00:35:14,016 --> 00:35:15,651
What do you mean?

641
00:35:16,252 --> 00:35:19,855
As her parents
we should be going there to pick her up.

642
00:35:22,325 --> 00:35:23,492
Fine.

643
00:35:23,559 --> 00:35:25,394
But I'll go instead.

644
00:35:38,808 --> 00:35:41,877
All right.

645
00:35:44,880 --> 00:35:46,215
The one I did the other day…

646
00:35:48,684 --> 00:35:50,853
Did your dad and mom like it?

647
00:35:56,626 --> 00:35:57,693
I didn't show it to them.

648
00:36:00,997 --> 00:36:01,864
I see.

649
00:36:12,341 --> 00:36:13,242
What's the matter?

650
00:36:16,879 --> 00:36:18,714
I worked so hard to make it,

651
00:36:21,484 --> 00:36:22,852
but I ended up destroying it.

652
00:36:45,308 --> 00:36:47,243
Even though I worked so hard on it.

653
00:36:55,217 --> 00:36:56,218
Nene, what is it

654
00:36:57,219 --> 00:36:58,120
that you want to do?

655
00:37:00,790 --> 00:37:02,024
I don't know.

656
00:37:18,040 --> 00:37:19,408
You can do whatever you want.

657
00:38:00,182 --> 00:38:01,650
You're not going to use gold?

658
00:38:08,624 --> 00:38:09,859
The truth is…

659
00:38:15,831 --> 00:38:17,767
my favorite color is blue.

660
00:38:26,842 --> 00:38:27,943
Okay.

661
00:38:38,254 --> 00:38:41,424
YUKANAI

662
00:38:48,564 --> 00:38:49,799
Good evening.

663
00:38:50,332 --> 00:38:51,167
Good evening.

664
00:38:53,135 --> 00:38:55,137
-Come in.
-Thank you.

665
00:38:57,807 --> 00:38:58,707
Um…

666
00:39:00,075 --> 00:39:01,644
she just fell asleep.

667
00:39:02,144 --> 00:39:03,879
Can you take her back tomorrow?

668
00:39:03,946 --> 00:39:05,514
I'm taking her back tonight.

669
00:39:05,581 --> 00:39:07,082
Please wait a second.

670
00:39:07,149 --> 00:39:08,784
-Nene is inside, right?
-Wait.

671
00:39:09,652 --> 00:39:12,288
Nene is saying
that she doesn't want to go home.

672
00:39:13,088 --> 00:39:13,923
What?

673
00:39:15,191 --> 00:39:17,560
She would never say something like that.

674
00:39:17,626 --> 00:39:18,627
That's probably because

675
00:39:20,262 --> 00:39:22,364
she can't bring herself to tell you that.

676
00:39:38,881 --> 00:39:41,717
She did a diamond art project.

677
00:39:45,488 --> 00:39:48,190
I told her to freely choose
whatever color she wants,

678
00:39:48,757 --> 00:39:52,094
but at first she would only try
to replicate the sample.

679
00:39:53,629 --> 00:39:55,998
It made me wonder if she was too afraid

680
00:39:56,065 --> 00:39:58,100
to express her own will.

681
00:40:01,070 --> 00:40:03,439
Even when I told her
to choose any color she wanted,

682
00:40:04,507 --> 00:40:06,175
she chose the brown that would make

683
00:40:07,042 --> 00:40:09,912
her dad happy
and the pink that her mom would like.

684
00:40:11,180 --> 00:40:13,916
What's the meaning behind that?

685
00:40:18,621 --> 00:40:20,523
I believe she's trying to do everything

686
00:40:20,589 --> 00:40:22,925
in order to please her parents.

687
00:40:27,463 --> 00:40:28,797
Does anything come to mind?

688
00:40:31,600 --> 00:40:34,770
My husband and I have discussions
about her quite often.

689
00:40:35,871 --> 00:40:38,040
He wants to send her to cram school,

690
00:40:38,541 --> 00:40:40,543
while I want her to take up the piano.

691
00:40:41,644 --> 00:40:44,880
We do clash over our differing viewpoints…

692
00:40:45,581 --> 00:40:49,652
But I personally believe
that the best approach is to simply let

693
00:40:49,718 --> 00:40:51,420
Nene do whatever she wants to do.

694
00:40:52,488 --> 00:40:54,590
And that it is my role as her parent

695
00:40:55,090 --> 00:40:57,059
to help her cultivate those talents.

696
00:40:58,427 --> 00:40:59,662
Her talents?

697
00:41:01,263 --> 00:41:03,999
She loves playing the piano.

698
00:41:11,774 --> 00:41:12,808
Nene.

699
00:41:26,121 --> 00:41:27,723
I hate the piano.

700
00:41:32,061 --> 00:41:34,697
I can never become as good as Big Sis,

701
00:41:37,399 --> 00:41:39,468
and honestly,
I don't want to play the piano at all.

702
00:41:41,403 --> 00:41:42,338
Then

703
00:41:43,038 --> 00:41:45,641
-why didn't you say so?
-There's no way I could.

704
00:41:46,675 --> 00:41:50,379
If I do, you and Dad
will start fighting again.

705
00:41:58,220 --> 00:41:59,888
Why don't we let her stay here tonight?

706
00:41:59,955 --> 00:42:00,789
No,

707
00:42:01,357 --> 00:42:03,726
we've already canceled our enrollment,
so it's okay.

708
00:42:03,792 --> 00:42:05,995
-But we don't mind at all--
-Tatsuki.

709
00:42:07,896 --> 00:42:09,098
It's okay.

710
00:42:13,202 --> 00:42:14,603
Are you sure?

711
00:42:18,307 --> 00:42:19,842
I'll go home.

712
00:42:23,245 --> 00:42:24,880
Sorry for bothering you late at night.

713
00:42:26,215 --> 00:42:27,049
Go get changed.

714
00:42:30,285 --> 00:42:31,320
Thank you.

715
00:42:52,708 --> 00:42:54,143
It's worrisome, isn't it?

716
00:43:13,228 --> 00:43:15,197
TACHIBANA

717
00:43:39,421 --> 00:43:41,290
Nene, what's wrong?

718
00:43:43,926 --> 00:43:44,860
Hey.

719
00:43:45,828 --> 00:43:48,731
Nene. Nene, open up.

720
00:43:53,736 --> 00:43:54,570
Mr. Tatsuki.

721
00:43:55,571 --> 00:43:57,372
Mr. Tatsuki! It's about Nene…

722
00:43:58,073 --> 00:43:58,907
‎What?

723
00:44:01,977 --> 00:44:02,845
Thanks for coming.

724
00:44:02,911 --> 00:44:03,746
No problem.

725
00:44:06,014 --> 00:44:08,650
I don't know what to do anymore.

726
00:44:17,326 --> 00:44:19,561
Don't come in here! Go away!

727
00:44:21,830 --> 00:44:24,666
Sora! Open the door, Sora!

728
00:44:27,369 --> 00:44:28,337
I

729
00:44:30,072 --> 00:44:31,173
don't know what to do either.

730
00:44:32,174 --> 00:44:33,542
What?

731
00:44:35,110 --> 00:44:35,944
But…

732
00:44:39,381 --> 00:44:40,916
I have to do something.

733
00:45:06,141 --> 00:45:07,543
PREVIEW OF THE NEXT EPISODE

734
00:45:07,609 --> 00:45:09,711
‎THIS DRAMA IS FICTION

735
00:45:09,778 --> 00:45:11,079
Subtitle translation by: Lili Morita

